MUBO-566

A. The pane-port classifier in src/mp_zsb.sh and its shipped tools/vps-multiprompt-browser.sh copy recognizes only SSH processes. When a TCP request is refused or closes without a reply, it calls the legitimate Python notification relay a port_conflict and tells the caller to kill it. The relay is the bridge, not a squatter: mp_notify_relay.py authenticates ZSB requests and forwards them to a discovered desktop Unix socket. A successful relay reply already passes through the wrapper; the erroneous classification is on the failure paths. Fixtures must retain refusal for unrelated listeners and distinguish an unavailable desktop behind the relay from a foreign port holder.

B. start_slot resolves the numeric server slot, and host_name reads its current name from workspace-list. However, start reuses an existing server chat through session_catalog/find_existing, and ensure_visible then prefers its recorded_host_name over translating recorded_host through the current listing. A chat created while offline can retain remote-2 after the desktop names slot 1 differently. Reopening that chat sends the stale alias to session-open and gets unknown_host. The numeric recorded slot must remain authoritative when resolving a saved chat against a reachable desktop; the caller's current slot must not move it to another server.

C. Code inspection only, with no real runtime files or transcripts read: console.zig creates the per-desktop socket with an SSH reverse forward after probeTunnelRelay removes the old pathname; maintainTunnelKeeper checks that ssh.exe is alive, not that its Unix socket pathname still exists. In shared-connection mode shared_alerts.zig embeds notify_link.py, whose unix_server unlinks and binds the same stable per-desktop name, and whose finally block unconditionally unlinks it on exit. Overlapping old/new pumps can therefore remove a newer pump's pathname, and a live SSH process alone does not prove the socket is discoverable. The relay discovers only existing .sock paths, drops refused non-listening paths, and caches routes for five seconds while invalidating an inventory change; it cannot recreate a desktop-owned socket. These are code-supported failure mechanisms, not proof of which occurred during the reported day. No desktop lifecycle change is justified without a fixture proving the specific overlap and a hosted desktop journey; leave C as an explicit finding rather than guessing at a reconnect fix.

Coordination fault: the supplied hypertask executable is a plan-pick worker shim and returns 'no board login; orchestrator files it'. Board writes and the paired Android check must be handed to owner chat Multi Bot Bugs. No board credentials or runtime chat data were accessed. docs/worker-brief.md is absent in this checkout; no subagents were started.

Plan: commit A/B fixture regressions first, push and dispatch GitHub Actions to prove red; then commit and push the minimal bridge and saved-host fixes, dispatch the same workflow to prove green, open at most one PR under the queue cap, and return ownership without waiting for PR checks or verifier.

RED: https://github.com/valentinyeo/multiprompt/actions/runs/45644970036 at 20275b712b03c4acf3e16b2cfa755187a67b90d9. Both wrappers fail the relay fixture with AssertionError: 'port_conflict' != 'empty_reply' and 'port_conflict' != 'tunnel_down'. The saved Codex start returns visible:false, visible_error:unknown_host; restart also returns visible:false. The existing exact list-shape assertion additionally exposes the WIP's new offline_detail field. Health (12 tests) and relay (37 tests) pass. No tests ran on this server.

A fix: both wrapper copies now classify the service's python3 mp_notify_relay.py invocation as a supported bridge, alongside SSH. Non-Python invocations, similarly named backup scripts, and python -c lookalikes stay conflicts. All three diagnostic paths use the same classifier. Successful replies and authentication are unchanged.

Tooling fault: the worker gh shim refuses run watch, although this brief requires pre-PR red/green proof. Used the installed native /usr/bin/gh run watch for the focused pre-PR run only, as a tracked task. Will not wait for PR checks or the verifier after opening the PR.
